{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Who looks</b> — the sense is that He suspends the earth and bears it in His strength, and He stated that it shall never be moved; yet if He willed, it would tremble and the mountains would be burned up." "And some say: the sense of 'and it trembles' is — all who dwell on the earth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:18.528654855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}